    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "FORM 0-71\nEXIT LOCATIONS\nSOUTHERN\nAIRWAYS\nMARTIN 404\nEVACUATION PROCEDURES\nForward\nCargo Door\nTO OUR PASSENGERS\nvar an and handle an are end\nsituation which might arise.\nAircraft emergencies are infrequent; however, pro-\ncedures have been established in advance as pre-\ncautionary measures.\n-in the in moron on to h\nven care.\nre yourself\nIn the event of an emergency, remain calm. Listen\nand follow carefully the instructions given by your\nStewardess or other Crew Members.\nSEAT BELTS\nSeat belts are provided for your safety and comfort.\nThey must be fastened securely during all taxiings,\ntakeoffs and landings. It is recommended that your\nseat belt be fastened at any time you are seated.\nSeats must be in an upright position during all:\ntakeoffs, and landings.\nSMOKING\nWhenever the \"NO SMOKING\" sign is on, all smokes\nare to be extinguished.\nLIFE VESTS\nLife Vests are located in a pouch under each seat\nfor use in the event of an emergency water landing.\nREGULATIONS PROHIBIT THE USE OF ANY AM OR\nFM RADIO OR TV RECEIVERS IN FLIGHT.\nDO NOT REMOVE THIS CARD FROM AIRCRAFT\nFORWARD CARGO DOOR\nThe Forward Cargo Door is\nequipped with an inflatable\nemergency evacuation slide.\nOperation Procedures:\n1. Rotate Handle in direction of\narrow to \"OPEN.\"\n2. Push door outward.\n3.\nGrasp Red Handle on floor and\npull to inflate evacuation slide\nEVACUATION SLIDE\nBefore using slide, remove high-\nheeled shoes.\nThe correct way to use slide is to\nsit on sill and push off, feet first.\nDo not hold onto sides of slide\nand in no instance jump onto it.\nWindow\nExit\nWindow\nExit\nWindow\nExit\nWindow\nExit\nWindow\nExit\nWindow\nExit\nPassenger\nCabin Door\nWINDOW EXIT OPERATION\nILGG\n/рын\n1. Insert Hand in Slot\n2. Pull Handle down\n3. Grasp Bottom and Top\nof Window\n4. Lift inward.\nBRACING POSITION"
